// x11 "Are You Open?" (script v2, 2026-10-25, docs/x11-are-you-open.md). Ross picked idea 1 of docs/ideas-small-business-owners.md: "yes, let's do the first one".
// Ross flips his shop's sign to CLOSED and Chuck's face smacks onto the glass; the face finds him in his car, at his bedroom window and in his bath until he opens at 4 AM, and Chuck is just looking.
// Ross is jack-tyler (as in x08-x10), Chuck jack-chris-boston (as in x10). Lines 4, 6, 7 and 9 come through glass: muffled in the render, not here.
// Format: see scripts/voice-gen.mjs (lines, directions) and scripts/voice-build.py (cast, plan, gaps, lead, tableSfx). Take k of a line uses direction k.
